    "text": "If $n=\\prod_{1\\leq i\\leq t} p_i^{k_i}$ is the factorisation of $n$ into distinct primes then let $ f(n)=\\sum p_i^{\\ell_i}, $ where $\\ell_i$ is chosen such that $n\\in [p_i^{\\ell_i},p_i^{\\ell_i+1})$. Furthermore, let $ F(n)=\\max \\sum_{i=1}^t a_i $ where the maximum is taken over all $a_1,\\ldots,a_t\\leq n$ such that $(a_i,a_j)=1$ for $i",
